section.p:
        The STextField maps to a getter method in the model component. 

        In the View: 


Create the STextField. 

STextField t = new STextField(); 



Set the selector string. Scope expects it's implementers to adhere to the JavaBean standard, 
            so if the getter method in the model is called getName(), then the selector string is "name". 

t.setSelector("name"); 



If you want a Scope Control to be issued when the user presses the Enter key to exit this STextField, specify the ControlID. 

t.setControlID(HelloController.GOT_NAME);
